{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "73c4d7b2-dcbc-4f20-862b-b8350ce42910",
    "name": "Spring Backend Kit API",
    "description": "Postman collection for the Spring Backend Kit REST API.\n\n## Quick start\n1. Start the stack with `docker compose up --build`.\n2. Import this collection into Postman.\n3. Run **Register User**. The request generates a unique `userEmail` when `generateNewUserEmail` is `true`.\n4. Read the verification token from `docker compose logs spring-backend`, then set the collection variable `verificationToken`.\n5. Run **Verify Email**, followed by **Login**. Login automatically stores `accessToken` and `refreshToken`.\n6. Run the profile, token, and observability requests as needed.\n\nFor password recovery, run **Forgot Password**, copy the reset token from the same service logs into `resetToken`, then run **Reset Password**.\n\nThe default registered account has the `USER` role. To test a successful admin request, authenticate with an account that has the `ADMIN` role and set `adminAccessToken`. The collection also contains an RBAC denial test that uses the normal user token.\n\nRequests send an `X-Request-Id` value and collection-level tests verify that the server echoes it. Destructive requests, such as profile deletion and logout, are grouped separately and run only when explicitly sent.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "pm.variables.set('requestId', `postman-${Date.now()}-${Math.random().toString(16).slice(2)}`);"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "pm.test('X-Request-Id response header is present', function () {",
          "    const requestId = pm.response.headers.get('X-Request-Id');",
          "    pm.expect(requestId).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
          "});"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
